  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Greeting people in Spanish",
     "texto": [
      "In Spanish there is one greeting that works at any time of day: **hola**.\n\nIf you want to be more precise, use the moment of the day:\n\n- **buenos días**: in the morning\n- **buenas tardes**: in the afternoon\n- **buenas noches**: in the evening and at night, and also when you go to bed\n\nTo say goodbye: **adiós** or **hasta luego**.\n\nAnd the two words that open almost every door: **por favor** and **gracias**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Good morning, good afternoon",
     "texto": [
      "Greetings with «buenos» or «buenas» agree with the word that comes after them:\n\n- **buenos días**: «día» is masculine, which is why it takes **buenos**\n- **buenas tardes** and **buenas noches**: «tarde» and «noche» are feminine, which is why they take **buenas**\n\nIt's the same rule as «el libro» and «la mesa»."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "Buenos días.",
       "alumno": "Good morning.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [
